1
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:13,918
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:17,004
Ah, summer's here again

3
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:19,924
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,010
Ah, summer's here again

5
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,596
It's come, it's arrived, here it is!

6
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,850
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,477
Here they come on the southern wind

8
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,730
Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs

9
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,733
At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!

10
00:00:37,942 --> 00:00:40,736
Ah, summer's here again

11
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:43,781
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,576
Ah, summer's here again

13
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:49,245
It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!

14
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:52,498
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

15
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:55,334
Here they come on the southern wind

16
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:58,337
Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts

17
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:02,842
At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:15,354
Here they come on the southern wind

19
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:21,861
Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach

20
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:24,322
Want you!

21
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,081
CLASH OF THE TOKYOITES!

22
00:01:43,466 --> 00:01:46,636
You're doing great, Junpei and Kappei!

23
00:01:47,053 --> 00:01:49,180
Oh, it's the ladies from the traffic police!

24
00:01:49,388 --> 00:01:51,098
Good luck to you too!

25
00:01:51,432 --> 00:01:53,017
Thanks! You can count on us!

26
00:01:53,226 --> 00:01:55,645
It's getting lively with all these portable shrines!

27
00:01:55,853 --> 00:01:58,022
A festival is supposed to be lively!

28
00:01:58,231 --> 00:02:00,066
It'll get much livelier than this.

29
00:02:00,274 --> 00:02:01,275
Oh, Reiko-san!

30
00:02:04,111 --> 00:02:07,031
The real festival is about to start.

31
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:10,159
"TOKYOITE PORTABLE SHRINE FESTIVAL"

32
00:02:23,548 --> 00:02:25,466
Wow, there are so many portable shrines!

33
00:02:25,675 --> 00:02:28,427
Of course! We're gonna carry them in a race.

34
00:02:28,636 --> 00:02:31,597
First team to reach the main shrine are the top Tokyoites!

35
00:02:31,806 --> 00:02:33,808
It's the main event of the festival.

36
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,686
Here he is! Hey, over here!

37
00:02:36,894 --> 00:02:37,687
You're late, Ryo-san!

38
00:02:37,895 --> 00:02:38,813
Sorry, sorry!

39
00:02:39,522 --> 00:02:41,524
I was starting to worry you weren't coming.

40
00:02:41,732 --> 00:02:46,988
Me too! Without you, our neighborhood wouldn't have won three straight titles.

41
00:02:47,196 --> 00:02:47,989
Wow!

42
00:02:48,447 --> 00:02:51,242
Ryo-san's the definition of a real Tokyoite!

43
00:02:52,577 --> 00:02:53,452
You think?

44
00:02:53,786 --> 00:02:56,622
For sure! The biggest Tokyoite around!

45
00:02:56,831 --> 00:02:58,457
You're the number one Tokyoite!

46
00:02:58,791 --> 00:03:00,793
The super-Tokyoite, Ryo-san!

47
00:03:01,168 --> 00:03:03,838
Long live the top Tokyoite in the universe!

48
00:03:05,339 --> 00:03:07,758
I love it when people are sincere!

49
00:03:07,967 --> 00:03:10,094
That guy is a Tokyoite?

50
00:03:10,303 --> 00:03:11,512
Don't make me laugh!

51
00:03:12,305 --> 00:03:15,725
Anyone who lets a little praise go to his head

52
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:17,894
doesn't deserve to be called a Tokyoite.

53
00:03:18,102 --> 00:03:18,811
What?

54
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:22,023
I've not seen you here before. Which neighborhood are you from?

55
00:03:22,523 --> 00:03:26,068
This man is Kin-san, the best Tokyoite around.

56
00:03:26,277 --> 00:03:28,738
He's helping out our neighborhood this year.

57
00:03:29,447 --> 00:03:30,197
What did you say?

58
00:03:30,781 --> 00:03:34,201
We're getting sick of you guys boasting about winning every year.

59
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:37,455
You're just a fake Tokyoite. I'll put you in your place!

60
00:03:37,955 --> 00:03:41,500
We'll see about that! You won't be laughing for long!

61
00:04:07,568 --> 00:04:08,444
Amazing!

62
00:04:18,371 --> 00:04:20,289
That guy is all talk.

63
00:04:20,915 --> 00:04:22,667
I knew you were no Tokyoite!

64
00:04:23,042 --> 00:04:25,586
Anyone can carry the front of a shrine.

65
00:04:25,795 --> 00:04:29,757
A true Tokyoite directs things from up top!

66
00:04:29,965 --> 00:04:31,425
I'll show him!

67
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:33,636
Wait, Ryo-san!

68
00:04:33,844 --> 00:04:36,389
A real Tokyoite stands on top of the shrine!

69
00:04:36,597 --> 00:04:40,976
I guess you're too scared since you're sitting down like that.

70
00:04:41,936 --> 00:04:44,271
Ha, you're meant to stand on one leg!

71
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:47,233
'Cause a real Tokyoite just loves being number one!

72
00:04:47,441 --> 00:04:49,235
So you wanna play rough, huh?

73
00:04:50,778 --> 00:04:51,737
How about this?

74
00:04:51,946 --> 00:04:54,657
If you can't do this, you can't say you're a Tokyoite!

75
00:04:55,991 --> 00:04:58,119
Handstands are nothing special!

76
00:04:58,327 --> 00:05:00,955
A Tokyoite does it... like this!

77
00:05:01,163 --> 00:05:03,958
That's nothing! I'll show you the real Tokyo style!

78
00:05:04,417 --> 00:05:06,460
No, this is the true Tokyoite way!

79
00:05:06,669 --> 00:05:08,963
Nonsense! Here's a genuine Tokyoite pose!

80
00:05:12,633 --> 00:05:14,343
This is the original Tokyoite stance!

81
00:05:14,552 --> 00:05:16,679
This is the ultimate Tokyoite style!

82
00:05:20,015 --> 00:05:21,350
Ryo-san, are you okay?

83
00:05:26,564 --> 00:05:28,816
We're in last place all of a sudden!

84
00:05:29,025 --> 00:05:30,818
That's 'cause you were being stubborn!

85
00:05:31,027 --> 00:05:32,445
Yeah! At this rate, we've no...

86
00:05:32,653 --> 00:05:33,696
Shut up!

87
00:05:33,904 --> 00:05:36,198
We'll have to use plan B.

88
00:05:38,492 --> 00:05:40,453
Let's go! Take the shortcut!

89
00:05:44,707 --> 00:05:47,585
We can't lose! Take the shortcut too!

90
00:05:52,131 --> 00:05:53,466
Truly exquisite.

91
00:05:53,674 --> 00:05:56,927
One, two! One, two! One, two!

92
00:06:01,891 --> 00:06:06,395
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

93
00:06:13,819 --> 00:06:15,196
One, two! One, two!

94
00:06:15,404 --> 00:06:16,280
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

95
00:06:16,489 --> 00:06:18,991
Stop following us! That's cheating!

96
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,117
Yeah, right!

97
00:06:20,326 --> 00:06:22,578
It's you lot that're blocking us!

98
00:06:22,787 --> 00:06:25,122
Damn it! That big mouth!

99
00:06:25,498 --> 00:06:27,416
Gotta shake them off. Speed up!

100
00:06:29,001 --> 00:06:31,128
After them! Don't let them get away!

101
00:06:47,978 --> 00:06:49,313
Almost there!

102
00:06:49,522 --> 00:06:51,440
We'll be crowned top Tokyoites again!

103
00:06:51,649 --> 00:06:54,193
I'm not gonna let a guy like you win.

104
00:07:05,329 --> 00:07:07,373
Yes! Victory is ours!

105
00:07:10,459 --> 00:07:12,253
Slow down, you idiots!

106
00:07:12,461 --> 00:07:14,255
We're gonna crash into the shrine!

107
00:07:14,463 --> 00:07:16,257
Too late for that!

108
00:07:16,465 --> 00:07:18,509
We've got too much momentum to stop!

109
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,476
Almost forgot!

110
00:07:47,204 --> 00:07:49,081
That lousy jerk!

111
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:50,583
Are you all right?

112
00:07:50,791 --> 00:07:52,626
Damn it!

113
00:07:52,835 --> 00:07:56,922
We didn't get our fourth victory in a row, we got scolded for destroying the shrine,

114
00:07:57,131 --> 00:07:58,924
and I'm soaked!

115
00:07:59,133 --> 00:08:00,259
This is a disaster!

116
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:02,970
And it's all that jerk's fault!

117
00:08:05,639 --> 00:08:06,974
Damn it!

118
00:08:07,183 --> 00:08:09,059
It's all that cretin's fault!

119
00:08:09,268 --> 00:08:11,520
"KAME NO YU BATHHOUSE"

120
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:14,273
You'd better not be going in here!

121
00:08:14,523 --> 00:08:17,026
I'll use whatever bathhouse I want!

122
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,029
Ryotsu...

123
00:08:22,698 --> 00:08:24,950
Move! You're blocking the door!

124
00:08:25,159 --> 00:08:27,286
No, you move!

125
00:08:27,494 --> 00:08:29,788
Looks like they forgot their manners.

126
00:08:34,293 --> 00:08:36,086
-Old man, here's your money! -Old man, here's your money!

127
00:08:37,421 --> 00:08:41,133
Uh... Ryo-san, I have to give you some change.

128
00:08:41,342 --> 00:08:42,801
I'll get in the bath first!

129
00:08:44,678 --> 00:08:48,182
The price to enter is 370 yen,

130
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:51,852
so your change comes to...

131
00:08:52,061 --> 00:08:54,563
Forget it! You can keep the change today!

132
00:08:54,772 --> 00:08:55,606
Huh?

133
00:09:00,152 --> 00:09:02,112
A true Tokyoite is always first in the bath!

134
00:09:02,655 --> 00:09:03,906
Move it!

135
00:09:04,990 --> 00:09:07,159
I'm getting in first!

136
00:09:14,583 --> 00:09:16,502
What's wrong? I heard a scream.

137
00:09:17,544 --> 00:09:18,545
Scream?

138
00:09:18,754 --> 00:09:20,589
I didn't hear any scream.

139
00:09:20,798 --> 00:09:22,258
He must've imagined it.

140
00:09:22,466 --> 00:09:23,258
But...

141
00:09:23,467 --> 00:09:25,010
You imagined it!

142
00:09:26,804 --> 00:09:30,474
Hang on... Weren't you both rushing to get in the water first?

143
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:35,938
I was just about to get in.

144
00:09:36,146 --> 00:09:37,940
Yeah, same here.

145
00:09:46,365 --> 00:09:47,574
Stop trembling!

146
00:09:47,783 --> 00:09:49,410
You'll cool the water down!

147
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,328
S-S-Same to you!

148
00:09:54,456 --> 00:09:57,793
Nakagawa, go help out in the boiler room!

149
00:09:58,002 --> 00:10:00,462
I'll catch a cold in this lukewarm water!

150
00:10:00,963 --> 00:10:02,464
O-Okay...

151
00:10:04,258 --> 00:10:06,343
What? Raise the temperature?

152
00:10:06,552 --> 00:10:08,762
Yeah, they said it's still lukewarm.

153
00:10:08,971 --> 00:10:12,558
That's odd. It should be pretty hot already.

154
00:10:16,270 --> 00:10:18,772
"WATER TEMPERATURE"

155
00:10:18,981 --> 00:10:22,526
It's starting to heat up just a little.

156
00:10:23,402 --> 00:10:26,822
You call this hot? Don't make me laugh!

157
00:10:27,031 --> 00:10:30,325
This is still lukewarm for a real Tokyoite!

158
00:10:32,119 --> 00:10:34,872
Nakagawa, the water's still nowhere near hot!

159
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,374
Throw more firewood into the furnace!

160
00:10:37,958 --> 00:10:39,543
It's not hot yet?

161
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,546
Ouch!

162
00:10:44,173 --> 00:10:46,300
It's over 60 degrees!

163
00:10:46,508 --> 00:10:48,719
It's way too hot for a bath!

164
00:10:49,178 --> 00:10:51,597
I said it's lukewarm, you hear me!

165
00:10:51,805 --> 00:10:53,640
I don't care how many degrees it is!

166
00:10:53,849 --> 00:10:57,186
To a real Tokyoite, this is as cold as ice water!

167
00:10:57,978 --> 00:10:59,980
Go back to the boiler room, now!

168
00:11:00,189 --> 00:11:01,440
Okay.

169
00:11:05,736 --> 00:11:07,488
It's still lukewarm!

170
00:11:07,696 --> 00:11:09,406
I'll have to hum to keep myself warm!

171
00:11:09,615 --> 00:11:11,492
Nakagawa, do something!

172
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:12,701
Y-Yes!

173
00:11:34,556 --> 00:11:37,518
This is foundry grade coke from Nakagawa Steelworks.

174
00:11:37,726 --> 00:11:40,729
It can be heated up to 10,000 degrees in an instant.

175
00:11:41,063 --> 00:11:42,356
I see.

176
00:11:51,323 --> 00:11:53,200
These bubbles are what I want.

177
00:11:53,408 --> 00:11:58,288
If the water isn't boiling, it doesn't feel like a real bath!

178
00:11:58,497 --> 00:12:00,290
You moron!

179
00:12:00,499 --> 00:12:03,836
Don't make a fuss just because the water's boiling.

180
00:12:04,044 --> 00:12:06,130
To a Tokyoite, this is still lukewarm!

181
00:12:13,262 --> 00:12:14,346
Look out!

182
00:12:22,604 --> 00:12:25,858
Ryotsu!

183
00:12:26,066 --> 00:12:27,109
Where are you?

184
00:12:29,069 --> 00:12:30,112
Oh! Found you!

185
00:12:30,821 --> 00:12:33,073
Are... Are you okay?

186
00:12:35,033 --> 00:12:38,120
A bath has to be explosive for a Tokyoite to enjoy it.

187
00:12:38,328 --> 00:12:39,621
Damn right.

188
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:42,332
This is nothing!

189
00:12:48,297 --> 00:12:49,673
I'm back!

190
00:12:50,632 --> 00:12:52,134
Has Ryo-chan come round yet?

191
00:12:52,342 --> 00:12:53,886
No, not yet.

192
00:12:56,847 --> 00:12:58,849
But I've bought some sushi for him...

193
00:13:00,392 --> 00:13:02,227
Hey, did someone say sushi?

194
00:13:02,436 --> 00:13:04,146
You were awake the whole time?

195
00:13:04,354 --> 00:13:06,982
The word "sushi" woke me up.

196
00:13:07,191 --> 00:13:09,234
A real Tokyoite can't resist sushi!

197
00:13:09,443 --> 00:13:11,695
As expected, you're invincible!

198
00:13:12,237 --> 00:13:15,657
At least put on some pants before you eat!

199
00:13:15,866 --> 00:13:17,701
Be a bit more considerate!

200
00:13:17,910 --> 00:13:20,871
That word is not in my dictionary!

201
00:13:21,079 --> 00:13:22,998
Thanks for the food!

202
00:13:25,042 --> 00:13:26,210
What's wrong?

203
00:13:26,668 --> 00:13:28,712
What the heck is this?

204
00:13:29,338 --> 00:13:31,507
What do you mean? It's an avocado roll.

205
00:13:31,715 --> 00:13:32,716
Avocado?!

206
00:13:33,258 --> 00:13:35,677
It's a type of sushi from the West Coast of America.

207
00:13:35,886 --> 00:13:39,223
It's the in-thing. Very healthy.

208
00:13:39,806 --> 00:13:43,518
The West Coast of America? Very healthy?

209
00:13:43,727 --> 00:13:44,728
Are you kidding me?

210
00:13:45,604 --> 00:13:49,733
Don't you know why the best sushi is called "Edo-style"?

211
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:57,407
Because it was made from fish caught in the bay back when Tokyo was called Edo.

212
00:13:57,950 --> 00:13:59,910
This isn't real sushi!

213
00:14:01,203 --> 00:14:04,122
What the heck are you doing, Ryo-chan?

214
00:14:04,331 --> 00:14:06,124
That was too far!

215
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:09,670
Reiko-san bought that sushi just for you!

216
00:14:11,004 --> 00:14:12,256
Even if she did,

217
00:14:12,464 --> 00:14:16,551
my body rejects any sushi that isn't real Edo-style.

218
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:20,430
Well then, buy us some Edo-style sushi instead.

219
00:14:21,139 --> 00:14:24,476
I want to see how it's different from the one I bought.

220
00:14:24,685 --> 00:14:28,480
Because until I taste the difference, I won't be able to forgive you!

221
00:14:37,489 --> 00:14:41,451
Fine! I'll show you what real sushi is like, damn it!

222
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,911
"KAMEARI COMMERCIAL DISTRICT"

223
00:14:46,498 --> 00:14:50,669
I wonder what Edo-style restaurant he's taking us to. I can't wait!

224
00:14:50,877 --> 00:14:53,839
Yeah, it's the first time he's treated us to a meal.

225
00:14:54,423 --> 00:14:57,217
Damn, my wallet wasn't prepared for this.

226
00:15:00,429 --> 00:15:01,847
There's a cheap-looking place.

227
00:15:02,055 --> 00:15:04,933
By the way, how much further is it?

228
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:06,852
We're almost there.

229
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:10,605
You're not taking us to that revolving sushi place, are you?

230
00:15:10,814 --> 00:15:14,234
Well, look who it is! Mr. Tokyoite himself!

231
00:15:15,152 --> 00:15:16,320
It's you from the festival!

232
00:15:16,528 --> 00:15:17,571
"DAIJIN SUSHI"

233
00:15:19,281 --> 00:15:21,658
That's who Ryo-chan was arguing with?

234
00:15:21,867 --> 00:15:23,327
You're a sushi chef?

235
00:15:23,535 --> 00:15:26,747
Damn right. Family's been in the business for 500 years!

236
00:15:26,955 --> 00:15:30,959
Toyotomi Hideyoshi used to come all the time in his younger days.

237
00:15:31,168 --> 00:15:33,587
And Tokugawa Ieyasu was a regular too.

238
00:15:33,795 --> 00:15:36,340
This the famous Daijin Sushi!

239
00:15:36,798 --> 00:15:38,467
Let's go, Nakagawa, Reiko.

240
00:15:38,675 --> 00:15:42,346
Our brains will rot if we keep listening to this big mouth!

241
00:15:43,013 --> 00:15:46,683
Hey, don't tell me you're heading for that revolving sushi place?

242
00:15:47,559 --> 00:15:49,436
We'll go wherever we want!

243
00:15:50,562 --> 00:15:52,814
I guess Tokyoites aren't what they used to be.

244
00:15:53,023 --> 00:15:55,692
Imagine making your juniors eat revolving sushi!

245
00:15:57,402 --> 00:16:00,197
Huh? Weren't we going to that restaurant?

246
00:16:00,822 --> 00:16:03,575
Not that one. We're going here.

247
00:16:03,784 --> 00:16:07,496
You'd better satisfy us to the fullest, sushi chef!

248
00:16:07,704 --> 00:16:11,208
Of course! You're talking to a real Tokyoite here!

249
00:16:19,883 --> 00:16:22,177
So, what do you guys want?

250
00:16:22,928 --> 00:16:25,681
This kind of place costs an arm and leg.

251
00:16:25,889 --> 00:16:27,682
I'd better pick the cheapest stuff.

252
00:16:28,725 --> 00:16:31,686
We have some delicious sea urchin, Miss.

253
00:16:31,895 --> 00:16:34,064
Okay, I'll have some of that.

254
00:16:34,272 --> 00:16:35,190
Is something wrong?

255
00:16:35,399 --> 00:16:37,943
N-No, nothing at all.

256
00:16:38,151 --> 00:16:39,653
I don't know what to choose.

257
00:16:39,861 --> 00:16:42,280
We have some really exquisite tuna, sir.

258
00:16:42,489 --> 00:16:43,407
Tuna for me then.

259
00:16:43,615 --> 00:16:45,158
Hey, you!

260
00:16:45,617 --> 00:16:48,537
What is it? Are you worried how much it'll cost you?

261
00:16:48,745 --> 00:16:50,163
Pathetic.

262
00:16:50,372 --> 00:16:53,667
A real Tokyoite doesn't go home till their wallet's empty.

263
00:16:54,334 --> 00:16:57,879
D-Don't be ridiculous! I just wanted to ask to use the toilet.

264
00:16:58,088 --> 00:16:59,256
It's over there.

265
00:17:00,632 --> 00:17:03,969
That sea urchin and tuna alone will cost me five thousand yen.

266
00:17:04,177 --> 00:17:07,347
Even if I stick with the cheap stuff,

267
00:17:07,556 --> 00:17:10,559
this is still gonna come to more than twenty thousand.

268
00:17:12,227 --> 00:17:15,647
I'd better find a way to get out of here, and fast!

269
00:17:16,314 --> 00:17:17,899
Here you go.

270
00:17:18,233 --> 00:17:20,402
I'm feeling a lot better now. Time to eat!

271
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:25,949
Son of a...!

272
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:29,619
He's recommending all the most expensive stuff!

273
00:17:29,828 --> 00:17:31,371
Okay, you asked for it...

274
00:17:32,289 --> 00:17:34,374
Hey, I'll have a dried gourd roll.

275
00:17:36,418 --> 00:17:37,377
A dried gourd roll, huh?

276
00:17:38,253 --> 00:17:41,882
There you go, the cheapest item on the menu.

277
00:17:42,090 --> 00:17:45,635
Now it's time to employ my nitpicking strategy.

278
00:17:47,471 --> 00:17:48,638
What the heck is this?

279
00:17:49,097 --> 00:17:50,640
What? It's a dried gourd roll.

280
00:17:51,892 --> 00:17:53,894
You call this a dried gourd roll?

281
00:17:54,102 --> 00:17:57,647
The seaweed is stale, and there's only one small strip of dried gourd!

282
00:17:58,190 --> 00:18:01,151
A real Tokyoite would never eat something so tiny!

283
00:18:02,068 --> 00:18:04,070
I can't believe this place is 500 years old.

284
00:18:04,279 --> 00:18:06,531
This isn't real Edo-style sushi.

285
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:08,783
Let's go, Reiko, Nakagawa.

286
00:18:09,117 --> 00:18:11,119
-O-Okay. -What about the check?

287
00:18:11,536 --> 00:18:13,163
That sign out there is a fraud.

288
00:18:13,371 --> 00:18:16,124
I don't need to pay for this phony Edo-style sushi!

289
00:18:18,335 --> 00:18:20,003
It worked!

290
00:18:20,212 --> 00:18:21,630
-Not so fast! -Uh-oh.

291
00:18:21,963 --> 00:18:24,549
That was just the appetizer.

292
00:18:24,758 --> 00:18:28,637
This is the real dried gourd roll!

293
00:18:34,059 --> 00:18:35,310
Now we're talking!

294
00:18:36,102 --> 00:18:39,940
A real Edo-style dried gourd roll has to be this big at least.

295
00:18:40,148 --> 00:18:42,526
I'm glad you like it.

296
00:18:42,734 --> 00:18:44,986
Damn! This guy is good.

297
00:18:45,445 --> 00:18:48,240
I'm not gonna let you have it all your own way.

298
00:18:48,573 --> 00:18:50,909
So, what'll you have next?

299
00:18:51,368 --> 00:18:54,079
Let's see... I think I'll have some of that sea urchin.

300
00:18:54,454 --> 00:18:56,581
Okay! Coming up, one Sea Urchin Battleship Roll!

301
00:18:57,582 --> 00:19:00,585
Nah, I'll have a Space Battleship Roll.

302
00:19:01,628 --> 00:19:03,088
A Space Battleship Roll?

303
00:19:05,382 --> 00:19:06,216
You can't make one?

304
00:19:06,633 --> 00:19:09,719
Nonsense! I can make anything!

305
00:19:09,928 --> 00:19:10,720
I'll be right back.

306
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:15,433
Let's see... Space battleship... Space battleship...

307
00:19:18,853 --> 00:19:21,022
That's it!

308
00:19:21,398 --> 00:19:22,983
Here you go.

309
00:19:25,443 --> 00:19:27,988
Just for you, one Space Battleship Roll!

310
00:19:28,613 --> 00:19:29,489
What the heck is this?

311
00:19:30,073 --> 00:19:32,993
Look at that gun turret and bridge. Pretty cool, huh?

312
00:19:33,743 --> 00:19:36,997
You idiot! No battleship has only one gun turret!

313
00:19:37,205 --> 00:19:40,208
This is a Space Destroyer Roll at best!

314
00:19:41,209 --> 00:19:43,753
S-sorry, I must've misheard you.

315
00:19:43,962 --> 00:19:49,050
Not many customers ask for the Sea Urchin Space Battleship Roll.

316
00:19:49,384 --> 00:19:53,221
Coming up, an honest-to-goodness Sea Urchin Space Battleship Roll!

317
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:00,604
N-Now we're talking!

318
00:20:00,812 --> 00:20:03,773
I finally feel like I'm eating real sushi.

319
00:20:04,107 --> 00:20:06,276
As expected of a Tokyoite, you know your stuff.

320
00:20:07,986 --> 00:20:10,780
And you'll eat it in one bite, right?

321
00:20:11,489 --> 00:20:13,867
That's the real Tokyoite way after all.

322
00:20:14,284 --> 00:20:16,494
Of course!

323
00:20:23,418 --> 00:20:24,878
What's next?

324
00:20:26,463 --> 00:20:30,300
Well... Maybe a side dish.

325
00:20:30,508 --> 00:20:32,719
There's nothing you can't make, right?

326
00:20:33,053 --> 00:20:35,138
I know, bonito on a string!

327
00:20:35,472 --> 00:20:37,390
B-bonito on a string, huh?

328
00:20:38,183 --> 00:20:40,310
Here, bonito on a string!

329
00:20:40,894 --> 00:20:42,604
A whole spiny lobster nigiri!

330
00:20:42,812 --> 00:20:43,855
Here you go!

331
00:20:44,648 --> 00:20:46,107
A kappa-shaped cucumber roll!

332
00:20:46,316 --> 00:20:47,317
Here it is!

333
00:20:48,026 --> 00:20:49,194
Curry and rice!

334
00:20:49,402 --> 00:20:50,820
How about some fish?

335
00:20:51,154 --> 00:20:53,031
Salmon with roe nigiri!

336
00:20:53,239 --> 00:20:54,199
Done!

337
00:20:54,407 --> 00:20:55,700
Fresh tuna on ohagi!

338
00:20:55,909 --> 00:20:56,993
Coming up!

339
00:20:57,202 --> 00:20:59,245
They're both as stubborn as each other.

340
00:20:59,454 --> 00:21:00,830
Like a pair of kids.

341
00:21:04,292 --> 00:21:05,919
So, what else do you want?

342
00:21:06,127 --> 00:21:07,504
I've still got plenty left.

343
00:21:07,712 --> 00:21:09,214
L-Let's see...

344
00:21:09,422 --> 00:21:11,591
How about a dancing octopus?

345
00:21:15,762 --> 00:21:16,596
It's alive!

346
00:21:16,930 --> 00:21:18,974
One octopus, dancing on some rice.

347
00:21:19,182 --> 00:21:21,101
Just what you asked for!

348
00:21:21,851 --> 00:21:23,853
Come on, eat up while it's still fresh!

349
00:21:24,604 --> 00:21:28,900
Yes, this is it! A real Tokyoite must try this at least once in their lifetime!

350
00:21:39,786 --> 00:21:42,288
Oh, maybe it's a bit too fresh!

351
00:21:44,457 --> 00:21:47,085
Damn it! I'll eat this thing, at any cost!

352
00:21:51,089 --> 00:21:53,425
Get off! I can't breathe!

353
00:22:01,224 --> 00:22:04,561
If you're an Edo-style octopus, stop wriggling around!

354
00:22:16,573 --> 00:22:18,616
A-Are you okay?

355
00:22:20,326 --> 00:22:21,327
Oww!

356
00:22:22,871 --> 00:22:24,789
Got you!

357
00:22:26,166 --> 00:22:28,126
What's going on?

358
00:22:28,710 --> 00:22:31,880
I'm stuffed!

359
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:34,132
Here's your check.

360
00:22:36,676 --> 00:22:38,428
Two million yen?!

361
00:22:38,762 --> 00:22:40,722
You're not saying it's expensive, are you?

362
00:22:40,930 --> 00:22:44,934
O-Of course not! I was just shocked at how cheap it is.

363
00:22:45,393 --> 00:22:47,479
You'll be paying in cash, I assume?

364
00:22:47,687 --> 00:22:49,063
Like a real Tokyoite.

365
00:22:49,272 --> 00:22:52,734
Damn right! I'll go get the money now.

366
00:22:52,942 --> 00:22:54,611
I'll be right back.

367
00:23:13,254 --> 00:23:17,509
Sorry, all I have is small change. Mind counting it up for me?

368
00:23:17,717 --> 00:23:22,388
It's always nice to have some change! Lucky me!

369
00:23:22,722 --> 00:23:24,599
I knew you'd be pleased.

370
00:23:24,808 --> 00:23:27,352
Us real Tokyoites understand each other well.

371
00:23:27,894 --> 00:23:28,978
That's right!

372
00:23:32,315 --> 00:23:35,276
Neither of them is laughing with their eyes.

373
00:23:35,485 --> 00:23:37,987
I wish they'd take it easy with this Tokyoite thing.

374
00:23:53,711 --> 00:23:56,339
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

375
00:23:56,548 --> 00:23:59,259
1 SHRINE, 2 PORTABLE SHRINES, 34 BONSAI TREES, 10 CARS,

376
00:23:59,467 --> 00:24:02,095
1 BATHHOUSE, 1 RESTAURANT, A LOT OF HOUSES

377
00:24:04,722 --> 00:24:05,682
W-What?

378
00:24:05,890 --> 00:24:08,518
Why am I handcuffed to Reiko?

379
00:24:08,726 --> 00:24:10,728
Huh? There's no key?

380
00:24:10,937 --> 00:24:15,024
So we're gonna have to live like this forever?

381
00:24:15,525 --> 00:24:17,026
I don't want to!

382
00:24:17,235 --> 00:24:19,487
NEXT EPISODE RYOTSU AND REIKO TOGETHER... FOREVER?

383
00:24:19,696 --> 00:24:21,781
Don't miss it!

384
00:24:33,001 --> 00:24:37,297
Let's keep smiling always

385
00:24:37,922 --> 00:24:41,551
Even when things go wrong

386
00:24:41,759 --> 00:24:46,014
Keep a pretty smile on your face

387
00:24:46,639 --> 00:24:51,102
And go out as if nothing happened

388
00:24:51,644 --> 00:24:55,148
Hey, show me your smile

389
00:24:55,356 --> 00:24:59,360
You did nothing wrong

390
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:03,781
Hey, show me your smile

391
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:07,493
Just like you did before, yeah

392
00:25:07,994 --> 00:25:12,123
I want you to smile always

393
00:25:12,832 --> 00:25:17,295
A woman with a frown isn't pretty

394
00:25:17,795 --> 00:25:23,343
So you should smile as soon as you can

395
00:25:24,135 --> 00:25:27,096
It's the grown-up thing to do

396
00:25:39,275 --> 00:25:44,072
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
